        "statement": "<p>A weather service stores monthly temperatures in wide form. <code>wide</code> has one row per city (column <code>city</code>, str) plus one column per month: <code>\"Jan\"</code>, <code>\"Feb\"</code>, <code>\"Mar\"</code> — month columns always appear in calendar order in the frame, and a table may cover any two or all three of them.</p><p>Implement <code>to_long(wide)</code> returning a DataFrame with exactly the columns <code>[\"city\", \"month\", \"temp\"]</code> (in that order): one row per city-month combination, with the temperature in <code>temp</code>. Rows are sorted by <code>city</code> ascending; within a city, months appear in calendar order (Jan before Feb before Mar).</p>",
        "constraints": [
          "Return a DataFrame with exactly the columns ['city', 'month', 'temp'] in that order",
          "One row per city-month pair — no pair repeated, none dropped",
          "Rows sorted by city ascending; within a city, months in calendar order (Jan, Feb, Mar)",
          "The input's month columns are always in calendar order; 'city' is the only other column"
        ],
        "examples": [
          {
