        "statement": "<p>Ticket batches land raw: each row of <code>batches</code> is one recorded batch with columns <code>team</code> (str), <code>day</code> (str — one of <code>\"Mon\"</code>, <code>\"Tue\"</code>, <code>\"Wed\"</code>) and <code>tickets</code> (int). The same team-day can appear in several batches, and some team-days never occur.</p><p>Implement <code>team_grid(batches)</code> returning a DataFrame with exactly the columns <code>[\"team\", \"Mon\", \"Tue\", \"Wed\"]</code>: one row per team sorted by <code>team</code> ascending, one column per day in that order, each cell holding the <b>total</b> tickets recorded for that team on that day (sum over batches). Team-days with no batches count as <b>0</b>. Every input contains at least one row for each of the three days somewhere in the table, so all three day columns always exist.</p>",
        "constraints": [
